### 10. **No HTTPS/TLS Configuration** (OWASP #02)
**Severity:** CRITICAL

#### Current Issues:
- Application doesn't enforce HTTPS
- Credentials transmitted in plaintext
- Man-in-the-middle attacks possible

#### Recommendation:
```javascript
const https = require('https');
const fs = require('fs');

// In production, use valid certificates
const options = {
  key: fs.readFileSync(process.env.SSL_KEY_PATH || './localhost.key'),
  cert: fs.readFileSync(process.env.SSL_CERT_PATH || './localhost.cert'),
};

// Redirect HTTP to HTTPS
if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production') {
  const httpApp = express();
  httpApp.use((req, res) => {
    res.redirect(`https://${req.header('host')}${req.url}`);
  });
  httpApp.listen(80);
}

// Create HTTPS server
https.createServer(options, app).listen(3000, () => {
  logger.info('Secure server running on port 3000');
});

// In development, use self-signed certificates:
// openssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:4096 -nodes -out localhost.cert -keyout localhost.key -days 365
