377	### 1.8 A10:2021 - Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)
378	**Severity: MEDIUM**
379	
380	**Issue:** If the application makes external requests, SSRF vulnerabilities are possible
381	- No validation of URLs before making requests
382	- Potential access to internal resources
383	
384	**Risk:**
385	```
386	Access to internal services
387	Data exfiltration from internal networks
388	Denial of service
389	```
390	
391	**Recommendation:**
392	```javascript
393	// ✅ Validate external URLs
394	const axios = require('axios');
395	const { URL } = require('url');
396	
397	app.post('/fetch-resource', async (req, res) => {
398	  const { url } = req.body;
399	  
400	  try {
401	    // Validate URL
402	    const parsedUrl = new URL(url);
403	    
404	    // Whitelist allowed protocols and domains
405	    if (!['http:', 'https:'].includes(parsedUrl.protocol)) {
406	      return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Invalid protocol' });
407	    }
408	    
409	    const allowedDomains = ['trusted-api.com', 'api.trusted.com'];
410	    if (!allowedDomains.includes(parsedUrl.hostname)) {
411	      return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Domain not allowed' });
412	    }
413	    
414	    // Make request with timeout
415	    const response = await axios.get(url, {
416	      timeout: 5000,
417	      maxRedirects: 1
418	    });
419	    
420	    res.json(response.data);
421	  } catch (err) {
422	    logger.error('SSRF attempt blocked', { url, error: err.message });
423	    res.status(400).json({ error: 'Invalid URL' });
424	  }
425	});
426	```
