### 9. **MEDIUM: No CORS Configuration**
**Category:** OWASP A01:2021 – Broken Access Control  
**Severity:** MEDIUM

**Issue:**
No CORS (Cross-Origin Resource Sharing) policy configured:

```javascript
// Current code allows any origin
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  res.json([...]);
});
```

**Risks:**
- Allows any website to access your API
- Vulnerable to CSRF (Cross-Site Request Forgery)
- May expose sensitive data to unauthorized origins
- No protection for browser-based clients

**Recommendations:**
```javascript
const cors = require('cors');

// Strict CORS policy
app.use(cors({
  origin: process.env.ALLOWED_ORIGINS?.split(',') || ['https://example.com'],
  methods: ['GET', 'POST'],
  allowedHeaders: ['Content-Type', 'Authorization'],
  credentials: true,
  maxAge: 3600,
}));

// Alternative: Manual CORS handling
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const allowedOrigins = ['https://example.com', 'https://app.example.com'];
  const origin = req.headers.origin;

  if (allowedOrigins.includes(origin)) {
    res.setHeader('Access-Control-Allow-Origin', origin);
    res.setHeader('Access-Control-Allow-Methods', 'GET, POST, OPTIONS');
    res.setHeader('Access-Control-Allow-Headers', 'Content-Type, Authorization');
    res.setHeader('Access-Control-Allow-Credentials', 'true');
  }

  if (req.method === 'OPTIONS') {
    return res.sendStatus(200);
  }
  next();
});
```

